### Supabase Service

#### [NEW] [SupabaseService.php](file:///d:/PROJECTS%20RANIEL%20CODES/laravel-game-vault/app/Services/SupabaseService.php)

A clean service class that wraps Supabase Auth REST API calls using Laravel's HTTP client:

```php
class SupabaseService
{
    public function signUp(string $email, string $password): array     // Register
    public function signIn(string $email, string $password): array     // Login
    public function signOut(string $accessToken): void                 // Logout
    public function getUser(string $accessToken): ?array               // Verify token
}
```

Each method uses `Http::withHeaders(...)` to call Supabase endpoints. Returns the parsed JSON response or throws on error.

---

### Auth Middleware

#### [NEW] [SupabaseAuth.php](file:///d:/PROJECTS%20RANIEL%20CODES/laravel-game-vault/app/Http/Middleware/SupabaseAuth.php)

Custom middleware that:
1. Checks if `supabase_user` exists in the session
2. If not → redirects to `/login` with a flash message
3. If yes → allows the request through, shares user data with all views via `View::share`

Registered as `supabase.auth` in the app's middleware aliases.

